course: dictionary
lesson: 4579
title: Helpdesk and getting help
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A helpdesk is a place, or a phone line, where people answer questions and fix problems. It is often about computers, but it can be any kind of help. «Call the IT helpdesk if a laptop breaks» tells you that the IT helpdesk is the people who fix computer problems.
explain: Read the words around the word. In «Others shift the blame: when a helpdesk says "user error", it means the machine is fine and the person using it got it wrong», the helpdesk is checking the machine and deciding what went wrong. The words «machine is fine» and «got it wrong» are clues that the helpdesk is judging the problem.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it in. Try "the people who fix problems" instead of helpdesk in «when the people who fix problems says "user error"». If it still makes sense, your meaning is probably right.
fact: A helpdesk is a service, desk or phone line where people answer questions and fix problems.
fact: Helpdesks are often about computers, such as the IT helpdesk at school or at work.
fact: You can also ask at a helpdesk in a shop or a library.
fact: Helpdesk can be written as one word or as two words: help desk.
fact: «User error» means the problem was caused by the person using the machine, not by a fault in the machine.
exercise: «Call the IT helpdesk if a laptop breaks.» What is an IT helpdesk for? | Lending library books to children | *Answering questions and fixing computer problems | Selling tickets for the football match | Baking cakes for the school fair
exercise: In the library, where could you ask for help finding a book? | On the bus | *At the helpdesk | Under the big table by the window | In the toilets
exercise: Miss Patel says, "Put in a helpdesk ticket for the broken printer." What should you do? | Post a letter to the head teacher | Write a note to your best friend | Ring your mum for a lift home | *Make a request for help to the helpdesk
test: «When a helpdesk says "user error", it means the machine is fine.» What does this tell you the helpdesk thinks? | The machine is broken | The helpdesk is closed | Nobody can be blamed | *The person using it made the mistake
test: Which sentence uses helpdesk correctly? | The helpdesk is a bright colour like blue | Helpdesk is a type of fish | Helpdesk means a holiday in the sun | *Ask at the helpdesk and they will help you find the book
exam: Which word best completes this sentence: "Call the ___ if the printer stops working." | Rainbow | Canteen | *helpdesk | Playground
